WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
One winter, storm after storm
swept in from the Atlantic.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.930
It was the wettest winter
in the UK's records:

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.290
165 per cent of average.

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.110
Summer 2003 was the opposite.

5
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.270
Rainfall was reduced across Europe,
and the UK brought in hosepipe bans.

6
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.890
Most of these weather systems
form over the Atlantic,

7
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.150
and move west to east.

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.010
So why does British
weather change so often,

9
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.230
yet sometimes stay
settled for weeks on end?

10
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.070
In this mission, you'll follow one
weather system across the country,

11
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.570
hour by hour.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.430
Then you'll see what brings calm,
settled spells that can last for weeks.

13
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.650
Your mission: explain why British
weather can change by the hour,

14
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.600
yet stay settled for weeks.
